# Simulation-only parameter defaults, layered on top of ArduPilot's own
# rover-skid.parm.
#
# A freshly built SITL refuses to arm with "3D Accel calibration needed":
# ArduPilot's prearm checks require an accelerometer calibration that a real
# vehicle receives during setup and a simulated one has never had. These are
# the nominal values ArduPilot's own automated tests use.
#
# Only two IMUs are calibrated here because SITL only simulates two. Adding a
# third block looks harmless but is not: ArduPilot then sees calibration data
# for an accelerometer that does not exist and fails the check outright, with
# the same "3D Accel calibration needed" message it was meant to fix.
#
# Note what this deliberately does NOT do: it does not disable ARMING_CHECK.
# The prearm checks stay fully enabled, so the simulator continues to refuse
# to arm for any reason a real vehicle would — a bad EKF, no GPS lock, a
# failsafe — which is exactly the behaviour worth testing against.

INS_ACCOFFS_X    0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Y    0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Z    0.001
INS_ACCSCAL_X    1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Y    1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Z    1.001

INS_ACC2OFFS_X   0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Y   0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Z   0.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_X   1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Y   1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Z   1.001
